# Docker matches a pattern without a slash only at the context root, so `server/.env`
# needs the **/ form. The build stage copies server/ wholesale, and an .env in a
# layer is an .env in the cache even if the final stage never uses it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
coverage
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
web/src/test
README.md
